t's  see let's do a couple more and then of  course you can always pause and and look  at the this whole presentation again so  you can get confused all over again  let's see let's do  minus 5 over seven  divided by  ten over three well this is the same  thing as minus five over seven  times  three over ten  i just multiplied by the inverse that's  all i keep doing over and over again  minus 5 times 3  minus 15  7 times  10  is 70.  if we divide the numerator and the  denominator by 5 we get minus 3  over 14.  we could have also just done it here we  could have done 5  2 and we've got minus 3 over 14 as well  let's do  one or two more problems  i think you kind of get it though  let's say  one half  divided by  minus three aha so what happens when you  take a fraction you divided by a whole  number or an integer well we know any  whole number can be written as a  fraction  this is the same thing as one-half  divided by  minus three over one  and dividing by a fraction is the same  thing as multiplying  by its numerator it's inverse  so the inverse of 3 negative 3 over 1 is  negative 1 over 3  and this equals negative 1 6.  let's do it the other way what if i had  negative 3  divided by  1 half same thing negative 3 is the same  thing as minus  minus 3 minus 3 over 1 divided by 1 half  which is the same thing as minus 3 over  1 times  2  over 1 which is equal to minus  6 over 1 which equals minus 6.  now let me give you a little bit of  intuition of why this works  let's say i said 2  divided by  1 3. well we know that this is equal to  2 over 1 times 3 over 1 which equals 6.  so how does 2 1 3 and 6 relate well  let's look at this way if i had two  pieces of pizza  i have two pieces of pizza here's my two  pieces of pizza  right two right here so i have two  pieces of pizza and i'm gonna divide  them  into thirds  so i'm gonna divide each pizza into a  third i'll draw a little mercedes sign  so i'm dividing each pizza into a third  right  how many pieces do i have let's see one  two three  four  five  six i have six pizzas so you might wanna  sit and and ponder that for a little bit  but i think it it might make a little  bit of uh  of sense to you  i always do one more just to  just to tire your brain  if i had negative  7 over 2 divided by  4 9  let's make it negative 4 9. well that's  the same thing as  minus 7 over 2  times minus 9  over 4 right i just multiplied by the  inverse of negative 4 9.  9 times 7 is equal to negative and 7  times negative 9 is positive 63  and 2 times 4 is 8.  hopefully i think you have a good idea  of how to divide by a fraction now and  you can you can try out  the the dividing fractions modules have  fun

